# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 7 — scripted Event.new() + at-watcher + emit (e!).
#
# Phase 7 of M6 stdlib exposes Event.new() at the scripted level.  The
# C-side machinery (urbi_event_create + UEvent GC cell + at_watchers
# linked list) shipped with M5 R5; Phase 7 wraps it as a Phase-3 native
# method on the Event proto and unifies vm->event_proto with
# vm->atom_event so atom-dispatch finds the methods.
#
# After Phase 7:
#   - var e = Event.new() returns a UVAL_EVENT.
#   - at (e?) body installs an AT_EVENT watcher subscribed to e.
#   - e! desugars to e.emit() and async-fires every subscriber body.
#
# The framed value of `var e = Event.new()` is <event> (the event
# value's display).  Each subsequent emit + Realm.counter pair pins
# the counter increment after the body strand drains.

# Construct the event and install the watcher.
var e = Event.new()
[00000000] <event>

at (e?) Realm.counter = Realm.counter + 1
[00000001] nil

# Initialize Realm.counter; framed value reads back cleanly.
Realm.counter = 0
[00000002] 0

# First emit: body fires once.
e!
[00000003] nil

Realm.counter
[00000003] 1

# Second emit: body fires again (no rising-edge gate on event watchers).
e!
[00000003] nil

Realm.counter
[00000003] 2

# Pair of emits: counter advances by 2.
e!
[00000003] nil

e!
[00000003] nil

Realm.counter
[00000003] 4
